SynapseIDS sensor for OPNsense.

Turns an OPNsense firewall into an inbound-WAN sensor for a central SynapseIDS
daemon. The plugin captures traffic on the selected interface through FreeBSD's
BPF devices and streams the raw frames to synapsed over SYNPOIP, the project's
framed, authenticated, TLS-only PCAP-over-IP transport. Flow assembly, feature
extraction and neural-network classification all happen on the daemon; the
firewall only observes and forwards.

Everything is configured from Services > SynapseIDS Sensor: capture interface,
filter preset, direction, the daemon address, the bearer token and the TLS
trust settings. The sensor runs as the dedicated unprivileged _synapseids
account with read-only access to the bpf devices, never as root, and never
modifies or injects traffic.

